; `checkNumericBoundsValue` reports the FIRST failure, and the order it
; checks in is a contract, not an accident. Each line below violates
; `:multiple-of 256` as well as something else, and the something else is
; what gets reported:
;
;   250.5  — also fractional. `:integer` is checked first, because a
;            fractional value's real problem is that it is fractional.
;   -256   — a genuine multiple of 256, but below `:min`. Range is checked
;            before divisibility, so "below minimum" wins.
;   250    — otherwise acceptable, so divisibility is what is left.
;
; Get the order wrong and an author chasing an alignment error is told to
; align a number that is not even whole yet.
(plugin :name gfx :version "1.0.0" :sjon "1.3"
  (value-kind :name aligned-offset
    :underlying number
    :numeric (numeric-bounds :min 0 :integer true :multiple-of 256))

  (form :name entry
    (key :name binding :type number)
    (key :name offset  :type aligned-offset :optional true)))

(entry :binding 0 :offset 250.5)
(entry :binding 1 :offset -256)
(entry :binding 2 :offset 250)
